The diagram shows the graph of $y = f'(x)$, the derivative of a function $y = f(x)$.
Classify the stationary points of $y = f(x)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$},
             xmin=-3.4, xmax=5.4, ymin=-5.6, ymax=6.8, samples=100, clip=false,
             xtick={-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4,5}, ytick={-4,-2,2,4,6}]
\addplot[smooth, thick, <->, domain=-2.16:4.16] {x*x - 2*x - 3};
\node[font=\small] at (axis cs:3.7,4.7) {$y=f'(x)$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
